1. LICENCE

rnetis is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3, and
under no later version.

The full licence text ships with the package: it is inst/LICENSE-AGPL-3.md in
the sources, and LICENSE-AGPL-3.md in the package directory once installed.

The additional terms in section 2 supplement that licence as its section 7
permits. They do not reduce the rights AGPL-3 grants.


2. ADDITIONAL TERMS UNDER AGPL-3 SECTION 7

These terms apply to the material in rnetis for which Griffin Dynamics LLC
holds copyright. They do not apply to the third-party material identified in
section 3 and in inst/COPYRIGHTS.

  (a) Warranty and liability — AGPL-3 section 7(a). To the fullest extent
      permitted by applicable law, the material is provided without warranty of
      any kind, and Griffin Dynamics LLC's liability is limited as far as the
      law allows, in addition to and not in place of AGPL-3 sections 15 and 16.

  (b) Preservation of notices and attribution — AGPL-3 section 7(b). Every
      copy, modified version and work containing the material must preserve,
      unaltered: the copyright notice above; this file; the AGPL-3 text
      (LICENSE-AGPL-3.md); COPYRIGHTS, including its identification of the
      third-party components and their copyright holders; the Authors@R field
      of DESCRIPTION; and the acknowledgements in DESCRIPTION, README.md and
      ?rnetis-package. Where a work containing the material displays
      Appropriate Legal Notices, it must display the copyright notice above
      among them.

  (c) Origin and marking of modified versions — AGPL-3 section 7(c).
      Misrepresenting the origin of the material is prohibited. A modified
      version must be marked, in a way a user will see, as changed from the
      original and as not the work of Griffin Dynamics LLC: it must carry a
      package name and a version string distinct from rnetis's, and state in
      its DESCRIPTION and on attach that it is a modified version not endorsed
      or supported by Griffin Dynamics LLC.

  (d) Publicity — AGPL-3 section 7(d). The names "Griffin Dynamics", "Griffin
      Dynamics LLC", "rnetis", and the names of the authors, contributors and
      acknowledged parties may not be used for publicity, endorsement,
      advertising or promotion of any product, service, work or modified
      version, without the prior written permission of Griffin Dynamics LLC.
      This includes implying that Griffin Dynamics LLC endorses, supports,
      supplies or has reviewed a modified version or a work containing the
      material.

  (e) Trademarks — AGPL-3 section 7(e). No rights are granted under trademark
      law. "Griffin Dynamics", "rnetis", the Griffin Dynamics logo, and any
      other trade name, trademark, service mark or logo of Griffin Dynamics LLC
      are expressly excluded from the licence. A redistributed or modified
      version must not use them, including in a package name, which is why (c)
      requires a distinct name. No mark, logo or trade name of any acknowledged
      party is used or redistributed with this package.

  (f) Indemnification — AGPL-3 section 7(f). Anyone who conveys the material,
      or a modified version of it, with contractual assumptions of liability to
      a recipient must indemnify Griffin Dynamics LLC and the authors for any
      liability those assumptions directly impose on them.

Each term above is one of the six that AGPL-3 section 7 permits, and each is
confined to material Griffin Dynamics LLC holds, as that section requires.


3. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

Parts of R/mgc-stats.R, R/mgc-prior.R and R/mgc-sampler.R derive from the R
package amen, copyright Peter Hoff, Bailey Fosdick, Alex Volfovsky and Yanjun
He, licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3. The hierarchical
Selection sampler also calls functions exported by amen at run time.

The GPL version 3 continues to apply to those parts. Section 13 of the GPL
version 3 and of the AGPL version 3 permits the combination.

inst/COPYRIGHTS identifies these components file by file, and installs as
COPYRIGHTS in the package directory.
